          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 36:2",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "It may be that the house of Judah will hear all the evil which I purpose to do unto them; that they may return every man from his evil way; that I may forgive their iniquity and their sin.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 36:3",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Jeremiah called Baruch the son of Neriah: and Baruch wrote from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the Lord, which he had spoken unto him, upon a roll of a book.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "Jer. 45:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Writing of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 45:1.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 45:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 45,
                    "end": 45,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 1,
